window.MORE=window.MORE||{};window.MORE.hha={"2":[["h202",1,["chest pain","doulè nan pwatrin"],["Kliyan an di: «Pwatrin mwen fè m mal.» Ki lè pou w rapòte sa?","Nan fen semèn nan, nan nòt chak semèn ou","Touswit; rele 911 si se yon ijans","Nan pwochen vizit ou","Sèlman si l di l ankò pita pandan vizit la","Doulè nan pwatrin ka yon ijans. Rapòte touswit epi rele 911 si siy yo grav."],["The client says, “My chest hurts.” When should you report it?","At the end of the week, in your weekly notes","Right away; call 911 if it is an emergency","At your next visit","Only if they say it again later in the visit","Chest pain can be an emergency. Report it right away and call 911 if the signs are serious."]],["h203",2,["document","ekri nan dosye"],["Ki lè pou w ekri swen ou bay nan dosye a?","Anvan w rive kay la","Nan fen semèn nan","Apre w fin bay swen an","Sèlman si gen yon pwoblèm","Ekri swen an apre w fin fè l. Pa janm ekri yon bagay ou poko fè."],["When should you document the care you gave?","Before you arrive at the home","At the end of the week","After you give the care","Only if there is a problem","Document care after you give it. Never record something you have not done yet."]],["h204",3,["correction","koreksyon"],["Ou fè yon erè nan nòt ou. Kisa ou fè?","Efase l","Kouvri l ak likid blan","Chire paj la","Swiv règ ajans ou pou korije l","Dosye a se yon dokiman legal. Swiv règ ajans lan pou koreksyon; pa janm efase ni kache sa w te ekri."],["You make a mistake in your note. What do you do?","Erase it","Cover it with correction fluid","Tear out the page","Follow your agency's policy to correct it","The record is a legal document. Follow agency policy for corrections; never erase or hide what you wrote."]],["h205",1,["subjective","subjektif"],["Kliyan an di w: «Mwen pa ka respire byen lannwit.» Kijan pou w ekri sa?","Kliyan an gen opresyon","Kliyan an di: «Mwen pa ka respire byen lannwit.»","Kliyan an konn twò pè","Pa ekri l paske se sèlman sa l di","Ekri sa kliyan an di ak pwòp mo l, ant gimè. Pa fè dyagnostik."],["The client tells you, “I can't breathe well at night.” How should you record it?","Client has asthma","Client says, “I can't breathe well at night.”","Client is too anxious","Do not record it because it is only what they said","Write what the client says in their own words, in quotes. Do not diagnose."]],["h206",2,["confidentiality","konfidansyalite"],["Yon zanmi w mande w kisa kliyan w lan genyen. Kisa ou di?","Di l si l pa pale sou sa ak lòt moun","Di l sèlman non maladi a","Pa pataje enfòmasyon sante kliyan an","Montre l foto dosye a","Enfòmasyon sante kliyan an konfidansyèl. Pataje l sèlman ak ekip swen ki bezwen l."],["A friend asks you what illness your client has. What do you say?","Tell them if they promise not to repeat it","Tell them only the diagnosis","Do not share the client's health information","Show them a photo of the record","The client's health information is confidential. Share it only with the care team members who need it."]],["h207",0,["baseline","sa ki nòmal pou kliyan an"],["Kisa ki ede w remake chanjman nan kondisyon yon kliyan?","Konnen sa ki nòmal pou li, nan plan swen an ak nòt anvan yo","Konpare l ak lòt kliyan w okipe ki gen menm laj","Mande vwazen yo","Tann fanmi an di w lè yon bagay sanble diferan","Ou ka remake yon chanjman sèlman si w konnen sa ki nòmal pou kliyan sa a."],["What helps you notice changes in a client's condition?","Knowing what is normal for them, from the care plan and earlier notes","Comparing them with other clients you care for who are the same age","Asking the neighbors","Waiting for the family to tell you when something seems different","You can only spot a change if you know what is normal for this client."]],["hha9",3,["observation","obsèvasyon"],["Ki pi bon nòt pou w ekri nan rapò vizit ou?","Kliyan an te move","Kliyan an te sanble parese e li pa t vle fè anyen jodi a","Mwen panse kliyan an deprime akoz fanmi an","Kliyan an manje mwatye manje midi l epi l mache 10 minit ak yon walker","Ekri fè ou wè epi ou mezire, pa opinyon. Nòt klè ede enfimyè a remake chanjman."],["Which is the best note to write in your visit record?","Client was in a bad mood","Client seemed lazy and did not want to do much today","I think the client is depressed because of the family","Client ate half of lunch and walked 10 minutes with a walker","Write facts you saw and measured, not opinions. Clear notes help the nurse notice changes."]],["h208",1,["social media","rezo sosyal"],["Ou vle poste yon foto ou pran lakay kliyan an sou rezo sosyal ou. Kisa ki kòrèk?","Pa gen pwoblèm toutotan figi kliyan an pa parèt nan foto a","Pa poste l: li ka devwale kliyan an, kay li oswa detay prive","Pa gen pwoblèm si w pa ekri non ni adrès kliyan an okenn kote","Pa gen pwoblèm si foto a montre sèlman bèt kliyan an oswa yon chanm","Menm yon foto bèt oswa yon chanm ka montre ki moun kliyan an ye, kote l rete oswa enfòmasyon sante l. Pa pran ni poste foto lakay kliyan san règ ajans ou pèmèt li."],["You want to post a photo you took in a client's home on your social media. What is correct?","It is fine as long as the client's face is not shown in the photo","Do not post it: it can reveal the client, their home or private details","It is fine if you do not write the client's name or address anywhere","It is fine if the photo only shows the client's pet or a room","Even a photo of a pet or a room can reveal who the client is, where they live or health information. Do not take or post photos in a client's home unless your agency's policy allows it."]],["h209",1,["change in condition","chanjman nan kondisyon"],["Kliyan w lan manje mwens pase dabitid jodi a, men sinon li santi l byen. Kilè pou w rapòte sa?","Rele 911 touswit, paske manje mwens se yon ijans","Nan fen vizit la oswa dapre règ ajans ou","Pa janm; sa pa enpòtan","Sèlman si sa dire yon mwa antye san l pa amelyore","Ti chanjman, tankou mwens apeti, rapòte nan fen vizit la oswa dapre règ ajans lan. Ijans tankou doulè nan pwatrin, rapòte touswit."],["Your client ate less than usual today but otherwise feels fine. When do you report it?","Call 911 right away, because eating less is an emergency","At the end of the visit or as your agency's policy says","Never; it is not important","Only if it lasts a whole month without getting better","Smaller changes, like less appetite, are reported at the end of the visit or by agency policy. Emergencies like chest pain are reported right away."]],["h210",3,["document","ekri nan dosye"],["Yon lòt ed mande w ekri nan dosye a ke li te benyen kliyan an, paske li te bliye. Kisa ou fè?","Ekri l, paske li di l te fè l e dosye a dwe konplè","Ekri l epi siyen non li","Ekri l pita nan semèn nan, lè w fin mande kliyan an","Pa ekri l; ekri sèlman sa ou menm ou fè oswa ou wè","Ekri sèlman sa ou menm ou fè oswa ou wè. Dosye a se yon dokiman legal."],["Another aide asks you to write in the record that she gave the client a bath, because she forgot. What do you do?","Write it, since she says she did it and the record should be complete","Write it and sign her name","Write it later in the week, once you have asked the client","Do not write it; write only what you yourself did or saw","Write only what you yourself did or saw. The record is a legal document."]]],"3":[["h302",2,["respiration","respirasyon"],["Poukisa ou konte respirasyon pandan dwèt ou toujou sou ponyèt la?","Pou w ka pran pou a ankò si w pèdi kont respirasyon yo","Pou w pa bliye","Pou kliyan an pa chanje fason l respire paske l konnen w ap konte","Paske li pi vit pase konte respirasyon yo apa","Si kliyan an konnen w ap konte respirasyon l, li ka respire diferan. Kite dwèt ou sou ponyèt la."],["Why do you count respirations while your fingers are still on the wrist?","So you can take the pulse again if you lose count of the breaths","So you do not forget","So the client does not change their breathing because they know you are counting","Because it is faster than counting the breaths separately","If the client knows you are counting their breaths, they may breathe differently. Keep your fingers on the wrist."]],["h303",0,["oral temperature","tanperati nan bouch"],["Kliyan an fèk bwè yon kafe cho. Konbyen tan pou w tann anvan w pran tanperati l nan bouch?","Omwen 15 minit","Ou pa bezwen tann","2 minit","2 èdtan","Bwason cho oswa frèt chanje tanperati nan bouch. Tann omwen 15 minit."],["The client just drank hot coffee. How long should you wait before taking an oral temperature?","At least 15 minutes","No need to wait","2 minutes","2 hours","Hot or cold drinks change the oral temperature. Wait at least 15 minutes."]],["h304",3,["thumb","pous"],["Ki dwèt ou pa dwe itilize pou pran pou?","Dwèt endèks","Dwèt nan mitan","Dwèt bag","Pous","Pous ou gen pwòp pou pa l, kidonk ou ka konte pa w olye pa kliyan an."],["Which finger should you NOT use to take a pulse?","Index finger","Middle finger","Ring finger","Thumb","Your thumb has its own pulse, so you might count yours instead of the client's."]],["h305",1,["fever","lafyèv"],["Tanperati kliyan an nan bouch se 100.6°F. Kisa ou fè?","Anyen, se nòmal","Rapòte l bay enfimyè a","Ba l yon grenn pou lafyèv","Tann pwochen vizit ou","100.4°F oswa plis ka vle di lafyèv. Rapòte l bay enfimyè a. Pa bay medikaman pou kont ou."],["The client's oral temperature is 100.6°F. What do you do?","Nothing, it is normal","Report it to the nurse","Give a fever pill","Wait until your next visit","100.4°F or higher can mean a fever. Report it to the nurse. Do not give medication on your own."]],["h306",1,["pulse","pou"],["Ki nivo pou nòmal pou yon granmoun k ap repoze?","40 a 60","60 a 100","100 a 140","140 a 180","Nòmal la se 60 a 100 batman pa minit. Rapòte sa ki pi ba oswa pi wo."],["What is the normal resting pulse range for an adult?","40 to 60","60 to 100","100 to 140","140 to 180","Normal is 60 to 100 beats per minute. Report lower or higher values."]],["h307",0,["respiration","respirasyon"],["Kisa yon respirasyon ye?","Pwatrin nan monte yon fwa epi desann yon fwa","Sèlman lè lestomak la monte, san konte lè l desann","Yon touse","Lestomak la monte de fwa youn dèyè lòt","Yon respirasyon gen yon monte ak yon desann pwatrin nan."],["What counts as one respiration?","The chest rises once and falls once","Only the chest rising, without counting the fall","One cough","The chest rising twice in a row","One respiration is one rise and one fall of the chest."]],["h308",2,["irregular","pa regilye"],["Pou kliyan an pa regilye. Kisa ou fè?","Konte 15 segonn epi miltipliye pa 4","Pa ekri l","Konte 60 segonn konplè epi rapòte l","Konte sèlman batman ki fò yo","Lè pou a pa regilye, konte pandan 60 segonn konplè epi rapòte l bay enfimyè a."],["The client's pulse is irregular. What do you do?","Count 15 seconds and multiply by 4","Do not record it","Count a full 60 seconds and report it","Count only the strong beats","When the pulse is irregular, count for a full 60 seconds and report it to the nurse."]],["h309",3,["blood pressure","tansyon"],["Ou pran siy vital yon kliyan: tanperati 99.0°F, pou 78, respirasyon 18, tansyon 190/110. Ki chif ki bezwen rapò touswit?","Tanperati a","Pou a","Respirasyon an","Tansyon an","Tanperati, pou ak respirasyon sa yo nan limit nòmal. Yon tansyon sistolik 180 oswa plis ka yon ijans: rapòte touswit, epi rele 911 si gen doulè nan pwatrin, souf kout oswa siy estwòk."],["You take a client's vital signs: temperature 99.0°F, pulse 78, respirations 18, blood pressure 190/110. Which reading needs reporting right away?","The temperature","The pulse","The respirations","The blood pressure","The temperature, pulse and respirations are in normal ranges. A top number (systolic) of 180 or higher can be an emergency: report it right away, and call 911 if there is chest pain, shortness of breath or stroke signs."]],["h310",1,["normal temperature","tanperati nòmal"],["Ki tanperati kò ki nòmal pou yon granmoun?","Anviwon 96.0°F (35.6°C)","Anviwon 98.6°F (37°C)","Anviwon 100.4°F (38°C)","Anviwon 102°F (38.9°C)","Anviwon 98.6°F (37°C) nòmal, epi li ka varye yon ti kras pandan jounen an. Rapòte 100.4°F oswa plis."],["What is a normal body temperature for an adult?","About 96.0°F (35.6°C)","About 98.6°F (37°C)","About 100.4°F (38°C)","About 102°F (38.9°C)","About 98.6°F (37°C) is normal, and it can vary a little during the day. Report 100.4°F or higher."]],["h311",0,["axillary (armpit) temperature","tanperati anba bra"],["Ou pran tanperati yon kliyan anba bra. Kisa pou w konnen?","Li bay yon chif ki pi ba pase nan bouch; ekri ke w te pran l anba bra","Li bay yon chif ki pi wo pase nan bouch","Li menm jan ak nan bouch, kidonk pa bezwen ekri anyen","Se sèlman pou timoun yo pèmèt sa","Anba bra bay yon chif ki pi ba. Swiv enstriksyon tèmomèt la epi toujou ekri ki kote w pran l."],["You take a client's temperature under the arm. What should you know?","It reads lower than by mouth; write down that you used the armpit","It reads higher than by mouth","It is the same as by mouth, so no note is needed","It is only allowed for children","The armpit reads lower. Follow the thermometer's instructions and always write down which site you used."]],["h312",2,["radial pulse","pou radyal"],["Ki kote w jwenn pou radyal la?","Sou kote kou a","Anndan pli koud la","Sou bò pous ponyèt la","Sou do pye a","Pou radyal la sou bò pous ponyèt la. Sèvi ak 2 oswa 3 dwèt, pa pous ou."],["Where do you find the radial pulse?","On the side of the neck","Inside the elbow","On the thumb side of the wrist","On top of the foot","The radial pulse is on the thumb side of the wrist. Use 2 or 3 fingers, not your thumb."]],["h313",3,["recheck","mezire ankò"],["Ou konte yon pou 118 epi ou pa sèten ou te konte byen. Kisa ou fè?","Ekri 100 paske li pre nòmal","Pa ekri anyen epi tann enfimyè a pran l pwochen fwa","Ekri yon chif ki nan mitan de kont ou yo","Mezire ankò, epi rapòte l bay enfimyè a si l toujou pa nòmal","Pa janm devine yon chif. Si w pa sèten, mezire ankò. Si l toujou pa nòmal, rapòte l."],["You count a pulse of 118 and are not sure you counted right. What do you do?","Write 100 because it is close to normal","Write nothing and wait for the nurse to take it next time","Write down a number halfway between your two counts","Measure again, and report it to the nurse if it is still abnormal","Never guess a number. If you are not sure, measure again. If it is still abnormal, report it."]],["h314",0,["systolic","sistolik"],["Yon tansyon se 130/85. Kisa 130 ye?","Chif sistolik la (anwo)","Chif dyastolik la (anba)","Pou a","Kantite respirasyon","Ekri de chif yo: sistolik se chif anwo a, dyastolik se chif anba a."],["A blood pressure reading is 130/85. What is the 130?","The systolic (top) number","The diastolic (bottom) number","The pulse","The breathing rate","Record both numbers: systolic is the top number and diastolic is the bottom number."]]],"5":[["h502",2,["stool","poupou"],["Ou remake poupou kliyan an nwa tankou goudwon. Kisa ou fè?","Anyen; sa nòmal pou pifò kliyan ki aje","Tann twa jou pou w wè si l chanje","Rapòte l touswit bay enfimyè a","Ba l plis fib","Poupou nwa oswa ak san ka siy senyen nan vant. Rapòte l touswit."],["You notice the client's stool is black and tarry. What do you do?","Nothing; it is normal for most older clients","Wait three days to see if it changes","Report it to the nurse right away","Give more fiber","Black or bloody stool can be a sign of bleeding in the gut. Report it right away."]],["h503",0,["sudden change","chanjman toudenkou"],["Yon kliyan ki toujou klè vin konfonn toudenkou jodi a. Kisa sa ye?","Yon chanjman toudenkou pou w rapòte touswit","Jis laj","Fatig nòmal","Yon bagay pou w note nan fen semèn nan","Yon chanjman toudenkou pa janm jis laj. Rapòte l touswit."],["A client who is usually alert is suddenly confused today. What is this?","A sudden change to report right away","Just aging","Normal tiredness","Something to note at the end of the week","A sudden change is never just aging. Report it right away."]],["h504",1,["urine output","kantite pipi"],["Kliyan an pipi pi piti pase dabitid epi pipi a fonse. Kisa sa ka vle di, e kisa ou fè?","Li bwè twòp dlo; retire dlo a","Li ka dezidrate; rapòte l","Se nòmal pou granmoun","Pa fè anyen","Mwens pipi ak pipi fonse ka siy dezidratasyon. Rapòte l bay enfimyè a."],["The client is urinating less than usual and the urine is dark. What could this mean, and what do you do?","Too much water; take water away","They may be dehydrated; report it","It is normal for older adults","Do nothing","Less urine and dark urine can be signs of dehydration. Report it to the nurse."]],["h505",3,["chest pain","doulè nan pwatrin"],["Kliyan an gen yon presyon nan pwatrin ki desann nan bra goch li, epi l ap swe. Kisa ou fè?","Ba l yon aspirin pou kont ou","Fè l kouche epi tann","Rele fanmi an","Rele 911, epi apre sa ajans ou","Doulè nan pwatrin ki gaye nan bra ak swe ka yon kriz kadyak. Rele 911 touswit."],["The client has chest pressure spreading to the left arm and is sweating. What do you do?","Give an aspirin on your own","Have them lie down and wait","Call the family","Call 911, then your agency","Chest pain spreading to the arm with sweating can be a heart attack. Call 911 right away."]],["h506",0,["mood","moral"],["Yon kliyan ki konn pale anpil pa vle pale, pa manje, epi rete nan kabann depi kèk jou. Kisa ou fè?","Rapòte chanjman nan moral la bay enfimyè a","Kite l trankil, l ap pase","Fòse l leve","Di fanmi an li parese","Yon chanjman nan moral ak konpòtman se yon chanjman nan kondisyon. Rapòte l."],["A usually talkative client has not wanted to talk, eat or get out of bed for several days. What do you do?","Report the change in mood to the nurse","Leave them alone; it will pass","Force them to get up","Tell the family they are lazy","A change in mood and behavior is a change in condition. Report it."]],["h507",2,["shortness of breath","souf kout"],["Kliyan an di l pa ka respire byen lè l kouche plat, sa ki pa t konn rive. Kisa ou fè?","Retire zòrye li yo","Di l pou l pa enkyete l","Rapòte l bay enfimyè a","Fèmen fenèt yo","Nouvo difikilte pou respire se yon chanjman ou dwe rapòte. Si l grav, rele 911."],["The client says they cannot breathe well when lying flat, which is new. What do you do?","Remove their pillows","Tell them not to worry","Report it to the nurse","Close the windows","New trouble breathing is a change you must report. If it is severe, call 911."]],["h508",1,["fall","tonbe"],["Kliyan an tonbe, li gen doulè nan ranch li epi li pa ka kanpe. Kisa ou fè?","Ede l remonte nan kabann pou l ka repoze","Pa deplase l; rele 911 ak ajans ou","Ba l yon grenn pou doulè","Mande l eseye mache kèk pa","Doulè nan ranch ak pa ka kanpe apre yon tonbe ka yon zo kase. Pa deplase l; rele èd."],["The client fell, has hip pain and cannot stand. What do you do?","Help them back into bed so they can rest","Do not move them; call 911 and your agency","Give a pain pill","Ask them to try walking a few steps","Hip pain and being unable to stand after a fall may mean a broken bone. Do not move them; call for help."]],["h509",2,["circulation","sikilasyon"],["Pandan w ap ede kliyan an abiye, ou remake zòtèy li frèt epi yo vin ble, sa ki nouvo. Kisa ou fè?","Fwote yo fò pou chofe yo","Mete pye l nan dlo cho","Rapòte sa bay enfimyè a","Anyen; pye konn frèt souvan","Dwèt oswa zòtèy frèt, pal oswa ble ka siy yon pwoblèm sikilasyon. Rapòte chanjman an."],["While helping your client dress, you notice their toes are cold and bluish, which is new. What do you do?","Rub them hard to warm them","Put their feet in hot water","Report it to the nurse","Nothing; feet are often cold","Cold, pale or blue fingers or toes can signal a circulation problem. Report the change."]],["h510",1,["incontinence","pipi sou li"],["Yon kliyan ki te toujou al nan twalèt poukont li kòmanse pipi sou li semèn sa a. Kisa ou fè?","Mete kouchèt pou li epi pa di anyen","Rapòte l bay enfimyè a kòm yon chanjman nouvo","Ba l mwens bagay pou l bwè","Di l fè plis efò","Pipi sou li ki fèk kòmanse se yon chanjman nan kondisyon. Rapòte l. Pa diminye likid li poukont ou."],["A client who has always used the toilet on their own has started wetting themselves this week. What do you do?","Put them in briefs and say nothing","Report it to the nurse as a new change","Give them less to drink","Tell them to try harder","New incontinence is a change in condition. Report it. Do not cut their fluids on your own."]],["h511",3,["normal aging","chanjman nòmal ak laj"],["Ki chanjman nan yon kliyan granmoun ou dwe rapòte, olye w di se laj?","Li mache yon ti jan pi dousman depi kèk ane","Li bezwen linèt pou li","Dijesyon l ralanti sou anpil ane","Li pa tande byen depi yè","Kèk bagay ralanti avèk laj. Chanjman ki rive vit, nan kèk èdtan oswa kèk jou, toujou bezwen rapò."],["Which change in an older client should you report, rather than call it normal aging?","Walking a little more slowly over the past few years","Needing reading glasses","Digestion slowing down over many years","Not hearing well since yesterday","Some things slow down with age. Changes that happen quickly, over hours or days, always need to be reported."]]],"6":[["h602",1,["fire","dife"],["Ou wè lafimen ak dife nan kizin kliyan an. Kisa ou fè an premye?","Eseye etenn li ak dlo anvan l gaye nan lòt chanm yo","Fè kliyan an soti nan kay la, fèmen pòt yo, epi rele 911 depi deyò","Rele ajans ou an premye pou yo di w kisa pou w fè","Ranmase papye kliyan an","Moun yo an premye: fè kliyan an soti, fèmen pòt yo pou ralanti dife a, epi rele 911 depi deyò."],["You see smoke and fire in the client's kitchen. What do you do first?","Try to put it out with water before it spreads to the other rooms","Get the client out, close doors behind you, and call 911 from outside","Call your agency first so they can tell you what to do","Gather the client's papers","People first: get the client out, close doors to slow the fire, and call 911 from outside."]],["h603",0,["night light","ti limyè lannwit"],["Kliyan an konn leve lannwit pou l al nan twalèt. Kisa ki pi bon pou anpeche l tonbe?","Ti limyè lannwit ak yon chemen ki debarase","Fèmen pòt twalèt la","Bay kliyan an pantouf ki glise","Etenn tout limyè pou l dòmi pi byen","Ti limyè lannwit ak yon chemen san anyen atè diminye risk tonbe lannwit."],["The client often gets up at night to use the bathroom. What best prevents falls?","Night lights and a clear path","Closing the bathroom door","Giving slippery slippers","Turning off all lights so they sleep better","Night lights and a clutter-free path lower the risk of falls at night."]],["h604",2,["unsafe situation","sitiyasyon danjere"],["Lè w rive, yon moun nan kay la sou, l ap rele epi l ap menase w. Kisa ou fè?","Rete pou w fini swen an","Diskite avè l","Kite kay la epi rele ajans ou","Fèmen tèt ou nan chanm kliyan an","Sekirite w enpòtan. Kite kay la, rele ajans ou, epi rele 911 si gen danje imedya."],["When you arrive, a person in the home is drunk, shouting and threatening you. What do you do?","Stay to finish the care","Argue with them","Leave and call your agency","Lock yourself in the client's room","Your safety matters. Leave, call your agency, and call 911 if there is immediate danger."]],["h605",1,["burn","boule"],["W ap fè manje pou kliyan an. Kijan pou w met chodyè yo?","Ak manch yo vire deyò, pou yo fasil pou pran","Ak manch yo vire anndan sou recho a","Sou kwen recho a","Pa gen enpòtans kijan yo plase","Manch vire anndan anpeche moun frape yo epi boule."],["You are cooking for the client. How should you place the pots?","With handles turned outward, so they are easy to grab","With handles turned inward on the stove","On the edge of the stove","It does not matter how they are placed","Handles turned inward keep people from bumping them and getting burned."]],["hha2",1,["fall prevention","prevansyon tonbe"],["Ki chanjman ki fè kay yon kliyan pi an sekirite kont tonbe?","Sire planche yo","Retire tapi ki glise epi debarase chemen yo","Etenn limyè koridò a pou ekonomize","Monte kabann nan pi wo","Tapi ki glise, fil elektrik ak dezòd lakòz anpil moun tonbe. Kenbe chemen yo pwòp ak bon limyè, epi siye sa ki tonbe atè touswit."],["Which change makes a client's home safest from falls?","Waxing the floors","Removing loose rugs and clearing walkways","Turning off hallway lights to save power","Raising the bed higher","Loose rugs, cords and clutter cause many falls. Keep paths clear and well lit, and wipe up spills right away."]],["hha3",2,["oxygen","oksijèn"],["Kliyan w lan itilize oksijèn lakay li. Ki règ ki pi enpòtan?","Mete tank lan nan solèy dirèk","Monte debi a lè l santi l fatige","Pa fimen ni pa gen dife toupre l","Kouvri tib la ak yon lenn","Oksijèn fè dife boule pi vit. Pa fimen, pa limen bouji ni dife toupre l, epi pa janm chanje debi a pou kont ou."],["Your client uses oxygen at home. Which rule matters most?","Keep the tank in direct sun","Turn up the flow when they feel tired","No smoking or open flames nearby","Cover the tubing with a blanket","Oxygen makes fire burn faster. No smoking, candles or open flames near it, and never change the flow rate on your own."]],["hha10",2,["burn","boule"],["Anvan kliyan w lan antre nan beny lan, kijan ou tcheke dlo a?","Mande kliyan an teste l ak zòtèy li","Sèvi ak dlo ki pi cho nan tiyo a pou touye mikwòb","Teste l ak yon tèmomèt beny oswa anndan ponyèt ou","Kite l koule pandan yon minit, apre sa li pare","Granmoun ka boule fasil epi yo ka pa santi chalè byen. Teste dlo a anvan yo antre."],["Before your client gets into the bath, how do you check the water?","Ask the client to test it with their toes","Use the hottest water from the tap to kill germs","Test it with a bath thermometer or the inside of your wrist","Let it run for one minute, then it is ready","Older adults burn easily and may not feel heat well. Test the water before they get in."]],["h606",1,["grease fire","dife grès"],["Yon ti dife pran nan yon pwela lwil sou recho a. Kisa ki pi an sekirite?","Voye yon tas dlo sou li pou etenn li vit","Glise yon kouvèti oswa yon plato sou pwela a, fèmen recho a, epi pa deplase pwela a","Pote chodyè a deyò vit pou dife a pa gaye nan kwizin nan","Vante l ak yon sèvyèt","Pa janm mete dlo sou dife lwil. Kouvri l pou koupe lè a, fèmen recho a, epi kite kouvèti a jiskaske l frèt. Si dife a gaye, fè kliyan an soti epi rele 911 depi deyò."],["A small fire starts in a pan of oil on the stove. What is safest?","Throw a cup of water on it to put it out quickly","Slide a lid or baking sheet over the pan, turn off the burner, and do not move the pan","Carry the pan outside quickly so the fire cannot spread in the kitchen","Fan it with a towel","Never put water on a grease fire. Cover it to cut off the air, turn off the burner, and leave the lid on until it cools. If the fire spreads, get the client out and call 911 from outside."]],["h607",0,["within reach","nan rive men"],["Kliyan w lan pase pi fò jounen an nan yon fotèy. Ki kote telefòn li dwe ye?","Nan rive men l","Nan kizin nan pou l chaje","Nan yon tiwa pou l pa pèdi","Avèk moun nan fanmi an ki vin vizite","Mete bagay kliyan an itilize souvan nan rive men l, ansanm ak telefòn nan, pou l pa oblije leve epi riske tonbe."],["Your client spends most of the day in a recliner. Where should their phone be?","Within their reach","In the kitchen so it can charge","In a drawer so it is not lost","With the family member who visits","Keep things the client uses often within reach, including the phone, so they do not have to get up and risk a fall."]],["h608",2,["spill","dlo atè"],["Kliyan w lan jete dlo atè nan kizin nan. Kisa ou fè?","Kite l seche poukont li","Mete yon sèvyèt sou li epi netwaye pita","Siye l touswit","Di kliyan an pase bò kote l","Siye dlo ki tonbe atè touswit. Yon planche mouye ka fè kliyan an glise epi tonbe."],["Your client spills water on the kitchen floor. What do you do?","Leave it to dry on its own","Put a towel over it and clean later","Wipe it up right away","Tell the client to walk around it","Wipe up spills right away. A wet floor can make the client slip and fall."]],["h609",1,["smoke detector","detektè lafimen"],["Ou remake detektè lafimen nan koridò kliyan an pa mache. Kisa ou fè?","Retire pil la nèt","Rapòte sa bay ajans ou","Anyen; se travay pwopriyetè a","Tann pwochen egzèsis dife","Detektè lafimen yo dwe mache. Rapòte si youn pa mache."],["You notice the smoke detector in the client's hallway does not work. What do you do?","Take the battery out for good","Report it to your agency","Nothing; it is the landlord's job","Wait for the next fire drill","Smoke detectors must work. Report any that do not."]],["h610",3,["space heater","chofaj elektrik"],["Kliyan an sèvi ak yon chofaj elektrik nan chanm li. Ki kote li pi an sekirite?","Bò kabann nan pou l rete cho","Anba biwo a toupre papye yo","Toupre rido yo","Lwen dra, rido ak papye","Kenbe chofaj elektrik lwen dra, rido ak papye, paske yo ka pran dife."],["The client uses a space heater in the bedroom. Where is it safest?","Next to the bed to keep them warm","Under the desk near papers","Close to the curtains","Away from bedding, curtains and paper","Keep space heaters away from bedding, curtains and paper, which can catch fire."]],["h611",0,["original container","bwat orijinal"],["Ou vle vide kloròks nan yon boutèy ji vid pou l pi fasil pou sèvi. Kisa ki kòrèk?","Kenbe pwodui netwayaj nan bwat orijinal yo, lwen manje","Pa gen pwoblèm si w ekri KLORÒKS sou boutèy la ak makè","Sa bon si w rense boutèy la anvan","Pa gen pwoblèm si w kenbe l nan pòt frijidè a","Kenbe pwodui netwayaj nan bwat orijinal yo, lwen manje, pou pesonn pa bwè yo oswa melanje yo pa erè."],["You want to pour bleach into an empty juice bottle so it is easier to use. What is correct?","Keep cleaning products in their original containers, away from food","It is fine if you write BLEACH on the bottle in marker","It is fine if you rinse the bottle first","It is fine if you keep it in the refrigerator door","Keep cleaning products in their original containers and away from food, so no one drinks or mixes them by mistake."]],["h612",2,["address","adrès"],["Poukisa ou dwe konnen adrès egzak kay kote w ap travay la?","Pou w ranpli fèy lè travay ou","Pou w di zanmi w kote w ye","Pou w ka bay li a 911 si gen yon ijans","Pou w voye lèt bay kliyan an","Konnen adrès egzak kote w ye pou w ka bay li si w rele 911."],["Why should you know the exact address of the home where you are working?","To fill out your timesheet","To tell your friends where you are","To give it to 911 in an emergency","To mail the client letters","Know the exact address where you are so you can give it if you call 911."]]],"7":[["h702",2,["stroke","estwòk"],["Kliyan an souri epi yon bò figi l tonbe, epi pawòl li melanje. Kisa ou fè?","Fè l kouche pou l repoze epi tounen gade l nan inèdtan","Ba l yon aspirin","Rele 911 touswit epi note ki lè siy yo te kòmanse","Tann pou wè si sa pase","Figi ki tonbe ak pawòl melanje se siy estwòk. Rele 911 touswit epi note lè a: tretman depann de tan an."],["The client smiles and one side of the face droops, and the speech is slurred. What do you do?","Have them lie down to rest and check on them in an hour","Give an aspirin","Call 911 right away and note when the signs started","Wait to see if it passes","A drooping face and slurred speech are stroke signs. Call 911 right away and note the time: treatment depends on it."]],["h703",3,["seizure","kriz"],["Kliyan an gen yon kriz (seizure). Kisa ou pa dwe fè?","Pwoteje tèt li","Retire bagay ki bò kote l","Gade konbyen tan l dire","Mete yon bagay nan bouch li","Pa mete anyen nan bouch yon moun k ap fè kriz. Pwoteje tèt li, retire bagay danjere, epi gade lè a."],["The client is having a seizure. What should you NOT do?","Protect their head","Move objects away from them","Time how long it lasts","Put something in their mouth","Never put anything in the mouth of a person having a seizure. Protect the head, clear the area, and time it."]],["h704",0,["fall","tonbe"],["Ou jwenn kliyan an atè. Li di li byen. Kisa ou fè?","Pa leve l poukont ou; gade si l blese, rele enfimyè a oswa ajans ou, epi rapòte tonbe a","Leve l mete l sou chèz la vit epi pa di anyen, paske l byen","Kite l atè a jiskaske yon moun nan fanmi an vin ede","Ba l yon grenn pou doulè","Pa leve yon kliyan poukont ou apre yon tonbe. Gade si l blese, rele pou èd, epi rapòte chak tonbe."],["You find the client on the floor. They say they are fine. What do you do?","Do not lift them alone; check for injury, call the nurse or agency, and report the fall","Lift them back into the chair quickly and say nothing, since they are fine","Leave them on the floor until a family member arrives to help","Give a pain pill","Do not lift a client alone after a fall. Check for injury, call for help, and report every fall."]],["h705",1,["heart attack","kriz kadyak"],["Ki siy sa yo ka montre yon kriz kadyak?","Grangou, swaf ak bouch sèk","Doulè nan pwatrin, souf kout ak swe frèt","Po k ap grate ak yon ti bouton sou bra yo","Dòmi twòp","Doulè oswa presyon nan pwatrin, souf kout, swe frèt ak kè plen ka siy kriz kadyak. Rele 911."],["Which signs can mean a heart attack?","Hunger, thirst and a dry mouth","Chest pain, shortness of breath and cold sweat","Itchy skin and a mild rash on the arms","Sleeping too much","Chest pain or pressure, shortness of breath, cold sweat and nausea can be heart attack signs. Call 911."]],["h706",2,["burn","boule"],["Kliyan an boule men l ak dlo cho. Ki premye swen an?","Mete glas sou li touswit pou boule a sispann","Mete bè oswa lwil sou li pou kalme l","Mete l anba dlo frèt k ap koule, epi rapòte l","Pete anpoul yo","Refwadi yon brili anba dlo frèt k ap koule. Pa mete glas, bè oswa lwil, epi pa pete anpoul yo."],["The client burns a hand with hot water. What is the first care?","Put ice on it right away to stop the burning","Put butter or cooking oil on it to soothe it","Cool it under running cool water, and report it","Pop the blisters","Cool a burn under running cool water. Do not use ice, butter or oil, and do not pop blisters."]],["h707",0,["bleeding","senyen"],["Kliyan an koupe dwèt li epi l ap senyen. Kisa ou fè?","Mete gan epi peze dirèkteman sou blesi a ak yon twal pwòp","Lave l ak alkòl touswit, san gan","Kite l senyen pou l netwaye","Mare yon garo byen sere anlè koupi a touswit","Pwoteje tèt ou ak gan, epi peze dirèkteman sou blesi a. Rapòte l; rele 911 si l pa sispann."],["The client cuts a finger and it is bleeding. What do you do?","Put on gloves and press directly on the wound with a clean cloth","Wash it with rubbing alcohol right away, without gloves","Let it bleed to clean it","Tie a tourniquet tightly above the cut right away","Protect yourself with gloves, and press directly on the wound. Report it; call 911 if it does not stop."]],["hha5",1,["emergency","ijans"],["Kliyan w lan pa reponn epi li pa respire nòmalman. Kisa ou fè an premye?","Rele fanmi kliyan an","Rele 911 epi swiv fòmasyon ijans ou","Ba l dlo","Tann 10 minit pou wè si sa pase","Rele 911 touswit. Kòmanse CPR si w fòme pou sa, epi avèti ajans ou."],["Your client does not respond and is not breathing normally. What do you do first?","Call the client's family","Call 911 and follow your emergency training","Give them water","Wait 10 minutes to see if it passes","Call 911 right away. Start CPR if you are trained, then notify your agency."]],["h708",1,["911 call","rele 911"],["Ou rele 911 paske kliyan w lan tonbe san konesans. Kisa pou w fè pandan apèl la?","Rakwoche vit apre w bay adrès la, pou yo vini pi vit","Bay adrès egzak la, sa k pase ak kondisyon kliyan an, epi rete sou liy lan","Kite kliyan an epi al tann anbilans lan deyò nan lari a","Rele ajans ou an premye, apre sa 911","Bay adrès egzak la, sa k pase ak kondisyon kliyan an, epi rete sou liy lan. Pa kite kliyan an poukont li. Rele ajans ou osito w kapab."],["You call 911 because your client collapsed. What should you do on the call?","Hang up quickly after giving the address, so they come faster","Give the exact address, what happened and the client's condition, and stay on the line","Leave the client and wait outside on the street for the ambulance","Call your agency first, then 911","Give the exact address, what happened and the client's condition, and stay on the line. Do not leave the client alone. Call your agency as soon as you can."]],["h709",3,["unconscious","pèdi konesans"],["Kliyan w lan t ap toufe epi kounye a li pèdi konesans. Kisa ou fè?","Kontinye frape do l pandan l chita nan chèz la","Ba l dlo pou manje a desann","Fè l chita epi tann li reveye","Rele 911, kouche l sou yon sifas plat, epi kòmanse CPR si w fòme","Si moun ki t ap toufe a pèdi konesans: rele 911, kouche l sou yon sifas plat, epi kòmanse CPR si w fòme."],["Your client was choking and now becomes unconscious. What do you do?","Keep hitting their back while they sit in the chair","Give them water to wash the food down","Sit them up and wait for them to wake","Call 911, lay them on a flat surface, and start CPR if you are trained","If a choking person becomes unconscious: call 911, lay them on a flat surface, and start CPR if you are trained."]],["h710",0,["seizure","kriz"],["Kriz kliyan w lan dire plis pase 5 minit. Kisa ou fè?","Rele 911","Kenbe l fò jiskaske l rete","Mete yon kiyè nan bouch li","Tann; kriz toujou rete poukont yo","Rele 911 si yon kriz dire plis pase 5 minit. Se pou sa ou gade lè a pandan chak kriz."],["Your client's seizure has lasted more than 5 minutes. What do you do?","Call 911","Hold them down until it stops","Put a spoon in their mouth","Wait; seizures always stop on their own","Call 911 if a seizure lasts more than 5 minutes. That is why you time every seizure."]],["h711",2,["recovery position","pozisyon sou kote"],["Kriz kliyan w lan fèk fini. Ki pozisyon pou w mete l?","Fè l chita touswit","Kouche plat sou do","Sou kote","Kanpe, pou l mache","Apre yon kriz, vire moun nan sou kote l."],["Your client's seizure has just ended. How should you position them?","Sit them up right away","Flat on their back","On their side","Standing, so they can walk it off","After a seizure, turn the person onto their side."]],["h712",1,["low blood sugar","sik ba"],["Kliyan w lan ki gen dyabèt toudenkou ap tranble, l ap swe, li konfonn, epi kè l ap bat vit. Kisa sa ka ye?","Fatig nòmal; kite l fè yon ti dòmi","Sik ba; swiv plan swen an epi rapòte l","Yon grip k ap kòmanse; ba l likid epi kite l repoze","Twòp dlo","Tranble, swe, konfizyon ak kè ki bat vit ka vle di sik ba. Swiv plan swen an, rapòte l, epi rele 911 si l pa reponn."],["Your client with diabetes is suddenly shaky, sweaty and confused, with a fast heartbeat. What may this be?","Normal tiredness; let them take a nap","Low blood sugar; follow the care plan and report it","A cold coming on; give fluids and let them rest","Too much water","Shaking, sweating, confusion and a fast heartbeat can mean low blood sugar. Follow the care plan, report it, and call 911 if they do not respond."]]],"8":[["h802",2,["immediately","touswit"],["Pou rapò abi, kisa «touswit» vle di dapre gid federal la?","Nan 24 èdtan apre w fin aprann sa","Anvan fen semèn nan, nan rapò chak semèn ou","San reta, osito w dekouvri l","Lè w gen tan","«Touswit» vle di san reta, osito posib apre w dekouvri sa."],["For reporting abuse, what does “immediately” mean in federal guidance?","Within 24 hours of finding out","By the end of the week, in your weekly report","Without delay, as soon as you discover it","When you have time","“Immediately” means without delay, as soon as possible after you discover it."]],["h803",0,["injury of unknown source","blesi orijin enkoni"],["Ou jwenn yon gwo mak blese sou bra kliyan an. Pesonn pa wè sa k te pase, epi kliyan an pa ka eksplike. Kisa sa ye?","Yon blesi orijin enkoni ou dwe rapòte","Yon bagay nòmal ak laj","Yon bagay ou pa bezwen ekri","Yon pwoblèm pou fanmi an sèlman","Yon blesi pesonn pa wè k ap fèt epi kliyan an pa ka eksplike se yon blesi orijin enkoni. Rapòte l touswit."],["You find a large bruise on the client's arm. Nobody saw what happened and the client cannot explain it. What is this?","An injury of unknown source that you must report","A normal part of aging","Something you do not need to record","A problem for the family only","An injury nobody saw happen and the client cannot explain is an injury of unknown source. Report it immediately."]],["h804",3,["verbal abuse","abi vèbal"],["Ou tande yon manm fanmi ensilte kliyan an epi menase pou l pa ba l manje. Kisa ou fè?","Pa okipe l; se zafè fanmi, se pa pa w","Mande moun nan fanmi an pou l pale pi ba bò kote kliyan an","Tann pou wè si sa rive ankò","Rapòte l touswit; se ka abi vèbal ak mantal","Ensilt ak menas privasyon ka abi vèbal ak mantal, menm lè se fanmi. Rapòte l touswit."],["You hear a family member insult the client and threaten to withhold food. What do you do?","Ignore it; it is a family matter, not yours","Ask the family member to speak more quietly near the client","Wait to see if it happens again","Report it right away; it may be verbal and mental abuse","Insults and threats of deprivation can be verbal and mental abuse, even from family. Report it immediately."]],["h805",1,["privacy","vi prive"],["Pandan yon beny nan kabann, kijan ou pwoteje vi prive kliyan an?","Kite pòt la louvri pou w ka tande fanmi an","Dekouvri sèlman pati w ap lave a epi kenbe rès la kouvri","Retire tout dra yo yon sèl kou pou w ka travay pi vit","Mande fanmi an rete nan chanm nan","Fèmen pòt ak rido epi dekouvri sèlman pati w ap lave a."],["During a bed bath, how do you protect the client's privacy?","Leave the door open so you can hear the family","Uncover only the part you are washing and keep the rest covered","Remove all the sheets at once so you can work faster","Ask the family to stay in the room","Close doors and curtains and uncover only the part you are washing."]],["h806",2,["dementia","demans"],["Yon kliyan ki gen demans mande w menm kesyon an plizyè fwa. Kisa ki pi bon?","Di l li te deja mande w sa","Pa reponn","Reponn ak kalm epi senp chak fwa","Diskite avè l pou l sonje","Reponn ak kalm epi senp. Diskite ka fè l pè oswa fache."],["A client with dementia asks you the same question many times. What is best?","Tell them they already asked","Do not answer","Answer calmly and simply each time","Argue so they remember","Answer calmly and simply. Arguing can upset or frighten them."]],["h807",0,["independence","endepandans"],["Kliyan an ka bwose cheve l pou kont li, men li pran tan. Kisa ou fè?","Kite l fè l epi ede l sèlman si l bezwen","Fè l pou li pou w ka fini pi vit","Di l pa gen tan","Sote etap sa a","Ankouraje kliyan an fè sa l kapab. Sa kenbe fòs li ak diyite l."],["The client can brush their own hair but it takes time. What do you do?","Let them do it and help only if needed","Do it for them so you finish faster","Tell them there is no time","Skip this step","Encourage the client to do what they can. It keeps their strength and dignity."]],["hha6",2,["neglect","neglijans"],["Dapre definisyon federal yo, kisa neglijans ye?","Pawòl, ekri oswa jès ki ensilte oswa ki imilye kliyan an","Pran oswa vòlè bagay lakay kliyan an","Pa bay kliyan an byen oswa sèvis li bezwen pou l pa soufri ni blese","Yon blesi pèsonn pa t wè k ap rive e kliyan an pa ka esplike","Neglijans se lè yo pa bay kliyan an sa l bezwen, tankou manje, swen oswa sekirite. Lòt repons yo se abi vèbal, vòl byen ak blesi orijin enkoni. Ou rapòte nenpòt nan yo touswit."],["Under the federal definitions, what is neglect?","Insulting or demeaning words, writing or gestures toward the client","Taking or stealing items from the client's home","Failing to give goods or services the client needs to avoid harm or suffering","An injury that nobody saw happen and that the client cannot explain","Neglect is failing to give the client what they need, such as food, care or safety. The other answers are verbal abuse, misappropriation of property and an injury of unknown source. You report any of them immediately."]],["h808",2,["right to refuse","dwa pou refize"],["Kliyan an di l fatige epi l pa vle benyen jodi a, menm si plan swen an di beny. Kisa ou fè?","Fè benyen an kanmenm, paske plan swen an mete l pou jodi a","Rele 911","Respekte desizyon l, mande poukisa, pwopoze yon lòt lè, epi rapòte refi a","Sote l epi pa di pèsonn, paske se kliyan an ki mande","Kliyan an gen dwa refize swen. Respekte l, pwopoze yon lòt lè oswa yon lòt opsyon, ekri refi a, epi rapòte l bay sipèvizè w oswa enfimyè a."],["The client says they are tired and do not want a bath today, even though the care plan lists one. What do you do?","Give the bath anyway, because the care plan lists it for today","Call 911","Respect the decision, ask why, offer another time, and report the refusal","Skip it and tell no one, since the client asked","Clients have the right to refuse care. Respect it, offer another time or option, document the refusal, and report it to your supervisor or the nurse."]],["h809",0,["validation and redirection","valide ak chanje sijè"],["Yon kliyan ki gen demans fache epi l di ou vòlè mont li. Ki pi bon repons lan?","Rete kalm, rekonèt santiman l, ede l chèche mont lan, oswa chanje sijè a dousman","Esplike fèm, e diskite si sa nesesè, pou pwouve w pa t pran l","Menase pou w kite travay la","Fouye tiwa ak sak li touswit devan l","Pa diskite ak yon moun ki gen demans. Rekonèt santiman l, rete kalm, ofri èd, epi chanje atansyon l dousman. Rapòte akizasyon an bay sipèvizè w."],["A client with dementia becomes upset and says you stole their watch. What is the best response?","Stay calm, acknowledge their feelings, offer to help look, or gently redirect","Explain firmly, and argue if needed, to prove you did not take it","Threaten to leave the job","Search their drawers and bags right away in front of them","Do not argue with a person who has dementia. Acknowledge the feeling, stay calm, offer help, and gently redirect. Report the accusation to your supervisor."]],["h810",3,["client property","byen kliyan an"],["Pandan w ap netwaye, ou jwenn yon bag anba kabann kliyan an. Kisa ou fè?","Kenbe l, paske l te pèdi","Mete l nan sak ou pou w remèt li semèn pwochèn","Jete l ak pousyè a","Remèt li bay kliyan an","Pandan vizit ou, pa kase, pa deplase, pa pran anyen ki pou kliyan an."],["While cleaning, you find a ring under the client's bed. What do you do?","Keep it, since it was lost","Put it in your bag to return next week","Throw it out with the dust","Give it back to the client","During your visits, do not damage, misplace or take anything that belongs to the client."]],["h811",0,["culture","kilti"],["Kliyan w lan priye anvan chak manje epi li pito yo prepare manje l yon fason espesyal pou rezon relijyon. Kisa ou fè?","Respekte pratik li epi prepare manje a jan l pito, dapre plan swen an","Mande l sote lapriyè a pou manje a rete cho","Kwit jan w kwit lakay ou, paske w konnen l bon pou sante","Mande fanmi an chanje abitid kliyan an","Respekte kilti, relijyon ak fason kliyan an renmen fè bagay yo, dapre plan swen an."],["Your client prays before every meal and prefers food prepared a certain way for religious reasons. What do you do?","Respect their practice and prepare food the way they prefer, within the care plan","Ask them to skip the prayer so the food stays warm","Cook the way you cook at home, since you know it is healthy","Ask the family to change the client's habits","Respect the client's culture, religion and the way they like things done, within the plan of care."]],["h812",2,["physical abuse","abi fizik"],["Dapre definisyon federal yo, kiyès nan sa yo ki abi fizik?","Di kliyan an li pa vo anyen","Pran lajan nan bous kliyan an","Pense kliyan an pou l fè vit","Pa bay kliyan an manje li bezwen","Abi fizik se nenpòt aksyon pou fè mal, tankou frape, souflete oswa pense. Lòt repons yo se abi vèbal, vòl byen ak neglijans."],["Under the federal definitions, which of these is physical abuse?","Telling the client they are useless","Taking money from the client's wallet","Pinching the client to make them hurry","Not giving the client food they need","Physical abuse is any action meant to cause harm or pain, such as hitting, slapping or pinching. The other answers are verbal abuse, misappropriation of property and neglect."]],["h813",1,["investigate","mennen ankèt"],["Ou sispèk yon moun nan fanmi an ap fè kliyan w lan mal. Apre w fin rapòte, kisa wòl ou ye?","Kesyone moun nan fanmi an pou w jwenn verite a","Ekri sa w wè ak sa w tande, ak lè a; pa mennen ankèt","Fouye kay la pou w jwenn prèv","Di vwazen yo pou yo veye","Ou pa mennen ankèt. Rapòte touswit epi ekri sa w wè ak sa w tande, ak lè a."],["You suspect a family member is hurting your client. After you report it, what is your role?","Question the family member to find out the truth","Write down what you saw and heard, and when; do not investigate","Search the home for proof","Tell the neighbors so they can watch","You do not investigate. Report immediately and write down what you saw and heard, and when."]]],"9":[["h902",2,["perineal care","swen zòn pèsonèl"],["Nan ki direksyon pou w netwaye zòn pèsonèl yon fanm?","Depi dèyè rive devan","Nan wonn","Depi devan rive dèyè","Nenpòt direksyon","Depi devan rive dèyè anpeche mikwòb poupou antre nan pipi epi lakòz enfeksyon."],["In which direction do you clean a woman's perineal area?","Back to front","In circles","Front to back","Any direction","Front to back keeps stool germs out of the urinary tract and prevents infection."]],["h903",1,["nail care","swen zong"],["Kliyan an gen dyabèt epi zong li long. Kisa ou fè?","Koupe yo kout","Pa koupe yo; rapòte bay enfimyè a","Mande fanmi an koupe yo","Rache po bò zong yo","Yon ti blesi ka grav pou moun ki gen dyabèt oswa move sikilasyon. Pa koupe zong yo: rapòte bay enfimyè a."],["A client with diabetes has long nails. What do you do?","Cut them short","Do not cut them; report to the nurse","Ask the family to cut them","Trim the cuticles","A small cut can be serious for people with diabetes or poor circulation. Do not cut the nails: report to the nurse."]],["h904",3,["dentures","dan atifisyèl"],["Kijan pou w netwaye dan atifisyèl yon kliyan?","Nan dlo k ap bouyi, pou touye tout mikwòb","Kenbe yo anlè anba dlo cho k ap koule","Mete yo nan yon napkin papye","Sou yon sèvyèt oswa yon basen dlo, ak dlo frèt oswa tyèd","Manyen dan atifisyèl sou yon sèvyèt oswa yon basen dlo pou yo pa kase si yo tonbe. Dlo cho ka defòme yo."],["How should you clean a client's dentures?","In boiling water, to kill all the germs","Holding them up in the air under hot running water","Wrapped in a paper napkin","Over a towel or basin of water, with cool or lukewarm water","Handle dentures over a towel or basin of water so they do not break if dropped. Hot water can warp them."]],["h905",0,["catheter bag","sak kateter"],["Ki kote sak kateter kliyan an dwe ye?","Pi ba pase vesi a, epi pa atè","Sou vant kliyan an","Pandye sou ba kabann nan pi wo pase kliyan an","Atè bò kabann nan","Sak la rete pi ba pase vesi a pou pipi pa retounen andedan, epi pa atè pou l rete pwòp."],["Where should the client's catheter bag be?","Below the bladder and off the floor","On the client's abdomen","Hung above the client on the bed rail","On the floor by the bed","Keep the bag below the bladder so urine does not flow back, and off the floor to keep it clean."]],["h906",1,["bath water","dlo beny"],["Pandan yon beny nan kabann, kilè pou w chanje dlo a?","Yon sèl fwa, nan fen benyen an","Lè l vin frèt, gen savon oswa sal, ak anvan swen zòn pèsonèl la","Janmen, pou kliyan an pa frèt pandan w ap tann","Sèlman si kliyan an mande w chanje l","Dlo frèt fè kliyan an frèt, epi dlo sal pote mikwòb. Chanje l lè l vin frèt, gen savon oswa sal."],["During a bed bath, when do you change the water?","Only once, at the very end of the bath","When it gets cool, soapy or dirty, and before perineal care","Never, so the client does not get cold while you wait","Only if the client asks you to change it","Cool water chills the client, and dirty water carries germs. Change it when it gets cool, soapy or dirty."]],["h907",1,["dizziness","toudi"],["Pandan douch la, kliyan w lan di li toudi epi li santi l fèb. Kisa ou fè an premye?","Fini vit pou l ka al kouche","Fè l chita touswit, epi rapòte sa","Kite l pou w al chèche yon vè dlo","Mete dlo a pi cho pou l chofe","Toudi nan douch ka fè moun tonbe. Fè l chita touswit, sou chèz douch la si genyen youn, rete avè l, epi rapòte sa."],["During a shower, your client says they feel dizzy and weak. What do you do first?","Finish quickly so they can lie down","Have them sit down right away, then report it","Leave them to get a glass of water","Make the water hotter to warm them up","Dizziness in the shower can lead to a fall. Have them sit down right away, on the shower chair if there is one, stay with them, and report it."]],["h908",3,["oral care","swen bouch"],["W ap fè swen bouch yon kliyan ki pa reponn. Kisa ki enpòtan?","Vide yon vè dlo plen nan bouch li pou rense","Mete dwèt ou nan bouch li pou netwaye","Panche tèt li dwat dèyè pou w ka wè dan yo","Vire tèt li sou kote epi sèvi ak ti kantite likid sèlman","Yon kliyan ki pa reponn ka toufe. Vire tèt li sou kote, sèvi ak ti kantite likid, epi pa janm mete dwèt ou nan bouch li."],["You are giving mouth care to an unresponsive client. What matters most?","Pour a full glass of water into the mouth to rinse","Put your fingers in the mouth to clean","Tilt the head straight back so you can see the teeth","Turn the head to the side and use only a small amount of liquid","An unresponsive client can choke. Turn the head to the side, use little liquid, and never put your fingers in their mouth."]],["h909",3,["bed bath order","lòd beny nan kabann"],["Pandan yon beny nan kabann, ki zòn ou lave an dènye?","Figi a ak kou a","Bra yo","Janm yo ak pye yo","Zòn pèsonèl la","Lave depi zòn ki pi pwòp yo rive nan zòn ki pi sal yo: figi, bra, pwatrin, vant, janm, do, epi zòn pèsonèl la nan fen."],["During a bed bath, which area do you wash last?","The face and neck","The arms","The legs and the feet","The perineal area","Wash from cleanest to dirtiest: face, arms, chest, abdomen, legs, back, then the perineal area last."]],["h910",0,["dry thoroughly","seche byen"],["Apre w fin lave pye kliyan an, kisa ki enpòtan?","Seche byen, sitou ant zòtèy yo","Kite yo mouye pou po a rete mou","Mete krèm ant zòtèy yo","Mete chosèt touswit pandan yo mouye","Seche byen, sitou ant zòtèy yo ak anba pli po yo."],["After washing the client's feet, what is important?","Dry them well, especially between the toes","Leave them damp so the skin stays soft","Put lotion between the toes","Put socks on right away while they are wet","Dry well, especially between the toes and under skin folds."]],["h911",1,["bath safety","sekirite nan beny"],["Kliyan w lan pa fèm sou pye l epi li chita nan basen an. Telefòn sonnen nan lòt chanm nan. Kisa ou fè?","Al reponn li vit","Rete ak kliyan an; pa kite l poukont li nan basen an","Mande kliyan an kenbe ba a pandan w ale","Kite plis dlo koule pou l okipe","Pa janm kite kliyan an poukont li nan basen an oswa douch la si sa pa an sekirite pou li."],["Your client is unsteady and sitting in the tub. The phone rings in another room. What do you do?","Go answer it quickly","Stay with the client; do not leave them alone in the tub","Ask the client to hold the grab bar while you go","Let more water run to keep them busy","Never leave the client alone in the tub or shower if that is not safe for them."]],["h912",2,["shampoo","chanpou"],["W ap lave tèt yon kliyan nan kabann. Kisa pou w fè?","Kite cheve a seche nan lè a pandan inèdtan","Vide dlo sou figi l pou rense pi vit","Kouvri je l ak yon ti sèvyèt epi seche cheve a vit","Sèvi ak dlo ki pi cho a pou cheve a pwòp","Kouvri je kliyan an ak yon ti sèvyèt, epi seche cheve a vit pou l pa frèt."],["You are washing a client's hair in bed. What should you do?","Let the hair air-dry for an hour","Pour water over the face to rinse faster","Cover their eyes with a small towel and dry the hair promptly","Use the hottest water so the hair gets clean","Cover the client's eyes with a small towel, and dry the hair promptly so they do not get chilled."]],["h913",0,["toenail care","swen zong pye"],["Kliyan an mande w koupe zong pye l. Plan swen an pa pale de sa. Kisa ou fè?","Pa koupe yo; di enfimyè a","Koupe yo ak atansyon","Koupe yo sèlman si yo sanble long","Mande yon moun nan fanmi an kenbe pye a pandan w ap koupe","Pa koupe zong pye si plan swen an pa mande l epi w pa fòme pou sa."],["The client asks you to cut their toenails. The care plan does not mention it. What do you do?","Do not cut them; tell the nurse","Cut them carefully","Cut them only if they look long","Ask a family member to hold the foot while you cut","Do not cut toenails unless the care plan calls for it and you are trained."]],["h914",3,["denture cup","bwat dan atifisyèl"],["Ki kote pou w sere dan atifisyèl kliyan an lè yo pa nan bouch li?","Vlope nan yon sèvyèt papye sou plato manje a","Sèk, nan yon pòch","Nan yon vè dlo cho sou tab bò kabann nan, pou yo rete pwòp","Nan yon bwat ki gen non kliyan an, ak dlo oswa likid tranpe","Sere dan atifisyèl nan yon bwat ki gen non kliyan an, ak dlo oswa likid tranpe."],["Where should the client's dentures be kept when they are out of the mouth?","Wrapped in a paper napkin on the meal tray","Dry, in a pocket","In a glass of hot water on the night table, to keep them clean","In a container labeled with the client's name, in water or soaking solution","Store dentures in a container labeled with the client's name, in water or soaking solution."]],["h915",1,["dressing","abiye"],["Kliyan an gen bò dwat li ki fèb apre yon atak serebral. W ap ede l mete chemiz li. Ki bra ou mete nan manch lan an premye?","Bra gòch la, bò ki fò a","Bra dwat la, bò ki fèb la","Nenpòt, depi l alèz","Kite l mete chemiz la poukont li","Abiye bò ki fèb la an premye: bra ki fèb la bezwen plis espas pou l antre nan manch lan. Pou dezabiye, kòmanse ak bò ki fò a."],["After a stroke, the client's right side is weak. You are helping him put on a shirt. Which arm goes into a sleeve first?","The left arm, the strong side","The right arm, the weak side","Either one, as long as he is comfortable","Let him put the shirt on by himself","Dress the weak (affected) side first: the weak arm needs the most room to get into the sleeve. To undress, start with the strong side."]]],"10":[["h1002",1,["walker","walker"],["Ki lòd kòrèk pou mache ak yon walker?","Janm ki fò a, walker a, janm ki fèb la","Walker a, janm ki fèb la, janm ki fò a","De janm yo anvan, apre sa walker a","Leve walker a twò lwen devan, epi kouri rive","Avanse walker a an premye, apre sa janm ki fèb la, apre sa janm ki fò a."],["What is the correct order for walking with a walker?","Strong leg, walker, weak leg","Walker, weak leg, strong leg","Both legs first, then the walker","Lift the walker far ahead, then hurry to it","Move the walker first, then the weak leg, then the strong leg."]],["h1003",2,["guarding","pwoteje"],["W ap ede yon kliyan mache. Ki kote pou w kanpe?","Devan l, kenbe de men l epi rale l","Sou bò ki fò a, yon ti kras devan l","Bò ki fèb la, yon ti jan dèyè l, men w sou senti mache a","Lwen l pou l gen espas","Kanpe bò ki fèb la, yon ti jan dèyè, pou w ka pwoteje l si l pèdi balans."],["You are helping a client walk. Where do you stand?","In front of them, holding both hands and pulling them along","On the strong side, slightly ahead of them","On the weak side, slightly behind, holding the gait belt","Far away to give space","Stand on the weak side, slightly behind, so you can protect them if they lose balance."]],["h1004",0,["dizziness","toudi"],["Kliyan an di l toudi lè l fin chita sou kwen kabann nan. Kisa ou fè?","Kite l chita oswa kouche ankò epi rapòte l","Fè l kanpe vit pou sa pase","Fè l mache pi vit","Ba l kafe","Toudi lè moun leve ka montre tansyon desann. Pa fè l kanpe: kite l repoze epi rapòte."],["The client says they are dizzy after sitting on the edge of the bed. What do you do?","Let them sit or lie back down and report it","Have them stand quickly so it passes","Have them walk faster","Give them coffee","Dizziness on rising can mean a drop in blood pressure. Do not stand them up: let them rest and report it."]],["h1005",3,["body mechanics","mekanik kò"],["Ki bon mekanik kò lè w ap ede yon kliyan?","Pliye nan ren epi kenbe jenou w dwat","Tòde do w pou w vire","Kenbe kliyan an lwen kò w, a longè bra","Pye w louvri, jenou pliye, do dwat, epi kliyan an toupre w","Yon baz lajè, jenou pliye ak do dwat pwoteje do w. Vire ak pye w, pa ak do w."],["What is good body mechanics when helping a client?","Bend at the waist and keep your knees straight","Twist your back to turn","Hold the client at arm's length, away from your body","Feet apart, knees bent, back straight, and the client close to you","A wide base, bent knees and a straight back protect your back. Turn with your feet, not your back."]],["h1006",1,["falling client","kliyan k ap tonbe"],["Kliyan an kòmanse tonbe pandan l ap mache. Kisa ou fè?","Kenbe l pou l rete kanpe kèlkeswa sa k rive","Rale l sou ou ak senti a epi desann li dousman atè","Lage l pou w pa blese","Rele fanmi an an premye, apre sa ede kliyan an","Pa eseye kenbe yon moun k ap tonbe kanpe: nou de ka blese. Desann li dousman atè, pwoteje tèt li, epi rapòte."],["The client starts to fall while walking. What do you do?","Hold them up and keep them standing no matter what","Pull them toward you with the belt and ease them to the floor","Let go to avoid getting hurt","Call the family first, then help the client","Do not try to hold a falling person up: you could both be hurt. Ease them to the floor, protect the head, and report it."]],["h1007",2,["gait belt","senti mache"],["Kijan senti mache a dwe sere?","Sere byen sere pou l pa ka bouje ditou","Lach ase pou w ka pase tout men w anba l","Ase pou w ka glise de dwèt anba l","Sou kou kliyan an","Senti a dwe sou rad la, nan ren, sere ase pou w glise de dwèt anba l."],["How snug should the gait belt be?","Pulled tight so it cannot move at all","Loose enough to slide your whole hand under it","Snug enough to slide two fingers under it","Around the client's neck","The belt goes over clothing at the waist, snug enough to slide two fingers under it."]],["hha11",1,["cane","bekiy"],["Kliyan an gen yon janm gòch ki fèb. Nan ki men li dwe kenbe bekiy li?","Men gòch","Men dwat","Nenpòt men","De men yo","Kenbe bekiy la nan men ki opoze ak janm ki fèb la. Li avanse ansanm ak janm ki fèb la pou bay plis sipò."],["The client has a weak left leg. Which hand should hold the cane?","Left hand","Right hand","Either hand","Both hands","Hold the cane in the hand opposite the weak leg. It moves forward with the weak leg to give more support."]],["h1008",3,["strong side","bò ki fò"],["Apre yon estwòk, bò dwat kliyan an fèb. Ki kote pou w mete chèz woulant lan pou yon transfè kabann rive nan chèz?","Sou bò dwat, bò ki fèb la, ak fren yo bloke","Nan pye kabann nan","Nenpòt bò, toutotan fren yo pa bloke","Bò gòch, bò ki fò a, ak fren yo bloke","Mete chèz la sou bò ki fò a pou kliyan an ka sipòte tèt li ak bò sa a pandan l vire. Toujou bloke fren yo."],["After a stroke, the client's right side is weak. Where do you place the wheelchair for a bed-to-chair transfer?","On the right, the weak side, with the brakes locked","At the foot of the bed","On either side, as long as the brakes are off","On the left, the strong side, with the brakes locked","Place the chair on the strong side so the client can support themselves with it while pivoting. Always lock the brakes."]],["h1009",2,["twisting","tòde do"],["W ap ede yon kliyan pase depi kabann nan rive sou yon chèz bò kote l. Kijan pou w vire?","Tòde ren w pandan w ap leve","Bese ak janm ou dwat","Vire tout kò w nan deplase pye w","Kenbe kliyan an lwen ou epi balanse l","Vire tout kò w ak pye w; pa tòde do w. Kenbe kliyan an toupre w."],["You are helping a client move from the bed to a chair beside it. How do you turn?","Twist at the waist while lifting","Bend over with straight legs","Turn your whole body by moving your feet","Hold the client at arm's length and swing them","Turn your whole body with your feet; do not twist your back. Keep the client close."]],["h1010",0,["two-person transfer","transfè ak de moun"],["Plan swen an di transfè a bezwen de moun, men ou poukont ou jodi a. Kisa ou fè?","Pa fè l poukont ou; mande ajans ou èd","Fè l poukont ou ak anpil atansyon","Mande kliyan an kanpe poukont li","Sote transfè a epi pa rapòte l","Mande èd si kliyan an twò lou oswa plan swen an mande de moun."],["The care plan says a transfer needs two people, but you are alone today. What do you do?","Do not do it alone; ask your agency for help","Do it alone, very carefully","Ask the client to stand up on their own","Skip the transfer and do not report it","Ask for help if the client is too heavy or the care plan calls for two people."]],["h1011",1,["gait belt","senti mache"],["Kliyan w lan gen yon tib manje nan vant li. Ki kote senti mache a ka ale?","Dirèkteman sou tib la, byen sere pou l pa glise","Pa sou tib la si plan swen an pa pèmèt sa; swiv plan an","Otou pwatrin nan, anba bra yo, olye de ren an","Anba rad la, sou po a","Mete senti mache a sou rad la, nan ren. Pa mete l sou yon blesi, yon tib oswa yon vant ki fèk opere si plan swen an pa pèmèt sa."],["Your client has a feeding tube in the abdomen. Where can the gait belt go?","Right over the tube, fastened tightly so it does not slip","Not over the tube unless the care plan allows it; follow the plan","Around the chest, under the arms, instead of the waist","Under the clothing, against the skin","Put the gait belt on over clothing at the waist. Do not put it over a wound, a tube or a recent abdominal surgery unless the care plan allows it."]],["h1012",3,["cane","bekiy"],["Lè w ap mache ak yon bekiy, kilè bekiy la avanse?","Anvan janm ki fò a, poukont li","Sèlman nan eskalye","Apre de janm yo","Ansanm ak janm ki fèb la","Kliyan an kenbe bekiy la bò ki fò a, epi bekiy la avanse ansanm ak janm ki fèb la."],["When walking with a cane, when does the cane move forward?","Before the strong leg, on its own","Only on stairs","After both legs","Together with the weak leg","The client holds the cane on the strong side, and the cane moves forward with the weak leg."]],["h1013",0,["dangling","chita sou kwen kabann"],["Poukisa kliyan an dwe chita sou kwen kabann nan kèk minit anvan l kanpe?","Tansyon l ka desann lè l leve vit","Sa chofe kabann nan pou pita","Sa ba w tan pou w ranje kabann nan pandan l chita","Pou l ka dòmi pi byen pita","Chita anvan kite kò a adapte l. Tansyon ka desann lè moun nan leve vit, epi sa ka fè l toudi."],["Why should the client sit on the edge of the bed for a few minutes before standing?","Blood pressure can drop when they get up quickly","It warms up the bed for later","It gives you time to make the bed while they sit","It helps them sleep better later","Sitting first lets the body adjust. Blood pressure can drop when rising quickly, which can cause dizziness."]]],"11":[["h1102",2,["pain","doulè"],["Pandan ROM, kliyan an di l gen doulè. Kisa ou fè?","Kontinye pou jwenti a vin pi soup","Fòse l yon ti kras plis","Rete epi rapòte l bay enfimyè a","Ba l yon grenn pou doulè","Pa janm fòse yon jwenti. Rete lè gen doulè epi rapòte l."],["During ROM, the client says it hurts. What do you do?","Keep going to loosen the joint","Push it a little further","Stop and report it to the nurse","Give a pain pill","Never force a joint. Stop when there is pain and report it."]],["h1103",1,["support the joint","sipòte jwenti a"],["Kijan pou w kenbe yon jwenti pandan ROM?","Pa pwent dwèt yo sèlman, pou w pa peze jwenti a","Yon men anwo jwenti a, yon men anba l","Pa manch rad oswa janm pantalon kliyan an","Ou pa bezwen kenbe l","Sipòte jwenti a ak yon men anwo epi yon men anba pou mouvman an rete lis epi an sekirite."],["How should you hold a joint during ROM?","By the fingertips only, so you do not press on the joint","One hand above the joint and one below it","By the client's sleeve or pant leg","You do not need to hold it","Support the joint with one hand above and one below so the movement stays smooth and safe."]],["h1104",3,["reposition","chanje pozisyon"],["Konbyen fwa yon kliyan ki pa ka deplase dwe chanje pozisyon?","Yon fwa pa jou, apre benyen maten an","Sèlman lè l mande","Chak 8 èdtan, chak fwa ekip la chanje","Omwen chak 2 èdtan, oswa jan plan swen an di","Chanje pozisyon souvan, omwen chak 2 èdtan, diminye presyon sou po a epi anpeche blesi presyon."],["How often should a client who cannot move be repositioned?","Once a day, after the morning bath","Only when they ask","Every 8 hours, at each change of shift","At least every 2 hours, or as the care plan says","Repositioning at least every 2 hours relieves pressure on the skin and helps prevent pressure injuries."]],["h1105",0,["float the heels","leve talon yo"],["Kijan pou w pwoteje talon yon kliyan ki rete kouche?","Mete yon zòrye anba mollèt yo pou talon yo pa touche kabann nan","Mete yon zòrye dirèkteman anba talon yo pou kousen yo","Fwote talon yo fò","Mete chosèt sere pou talon yo rete cho","Leve talon yo ak yon zòrye anba mollèt yo pou yo pa peze kabann nan."],["How do you protect the heels of a client who stays in bed?","Put a pillow under the calves so the heels do not touch the bed","Put a pillow directly under the heels to cushion them","Rub the heels hard","Put on tight socks so the heels stay warm","Float the heels with a pillow under the calves so they do not press on the bed."]],["h1106",2,["side-lying","sou kote"],["Lè kliyan an kouche sou kote, ki kote pou w mete yon zòrye?","Anba tèt la sèlman, okenn lòt kote","Sou vant lan, anba bra ki anlè a","Ant jenou yo ak dèyè do a","Pa gen zòrye","Yon zòrye ant jenou yo anpeche zo yo peze youn sou lòt, epi youn dèyè do a kenbe pozisyon an."],["When the client lies on their side, where do you place a pillow?","Under the head only, and nowhere else","On the stomach, under the top arm","Between the knees and behind the back","No pillows","A pillow between the knees keeps the bones from pressing together, and one behind the back holds the position."]],["h1107",1,["Fowler's","Fowler"],["Ki pozisyon ki bon pou yon kliyan manje oswa respire pi byen nan kabann?","Kouche plat sou do, san zòrye","Fowler, tèt kabann nan leve","Sou vant","Tèt la pi ba pase pye yo, pou kè a repoze","Pozisyon Fowler, ak tèt kabann nan leve, ede kliyan an manje an sekirite epi respire pi fasil."],["Which position helps a client eat or breathe better in bed?","Flat on the back, with no pillow","Fowler's, with the head of the bed raised","On the stomach","Head lower than the feet, to rest the heart","Fowler's position, with the head of the bed raised, helps the client eat safely and breathe more easily."]],["h1108",3,["draw sheet","dra pou leve"],["W ap monte yon kliyan pi wo nan kabann nan. Kijan pou w fè l?","Rale l pa bra l","Rale l sou dra a poukont ou","Pouse l pa pye l","Sèvi ak yon dra pou leve (draw sheet) ak yon lòt moun","Rale kliyan an sou dra yo ka chire po a. Sèvi ak yon dra pou leve ak yon lòt moun, epi pa janm rale pa bra yo."],["You are moving a client up in bed. How should you do it?","Pull them by the arms","Drag them on the sheet alone","Push them by the feet","Use a draw sheet with a second person","Dragging the client on the sheets can tear the skin. Use a draw sheet with a second person, and never pull by the arms."]],["h1109",1,["care plan exercises","egzèsis plan swen an"],["Kliyan w lan mande w ajoute kèk nouvo egzèsis li wè nan televizyon. Kisa ou fè?","Ajoute yo si yo sanble fasil e san danje pou ou","Fè sèlman egzèsis ki nan plan swen an, epi di enfimyè a sa l mande","Ranplase egzèsis plan an ak nouvo yo kliyan an pi renmen","Fè yo de fwa plis pou l refè pi vit","Swiv sèlman egzèsis ki nan plan swen an, jan terapis la oswa enfimyè a ekri yo. Di enfimyè a sa kliyan an mande."],["Your client asks you to add some new exercises they saw on TV. What do you do?","Add them if they look easy and safe to you","Do only the exercises in the care plan, and tell the nurse about the request","Replace the plan's exercises with the new ones the client prefers","Do them twice as often to recover faster","Do only the exercises in the care plan, as the therapist or nurse wrote them. Tell the nurse about the request."]],["h1110",2,["active-assisted ROM","ROM aktif ak èd"],["Kliyan an leve bra l mwatye chemen epi ou ede l fini mouvman an. Ki kalite ranje mouvman sa a ye?","Pasif","Aktif","Aktif ak èd","Ak rezistans","Aktif ak èd vle di kliyan an fè yon pati nan mouvman an epi ou ede l fini l."],["The client raises their arm halfway and you help them finish the movement. What type of range of motion is this?","Passive","Active","Active-assisted","Resistive","Active-assisted means the client does part of the movement and you help finish it."]],["h1111",3,["force a joint","fòse yon jwenti"],["Pandan ranje mouvman, jenou kliyan an sispann pliye anvan kote l konn rive. Kisa ou fè?","Pouse yon ti jan pi fò pou rive kote l konn rive","Souke jwenti a pou l lache","Mande kliyan an fòse","Rete la; pa janm fòse yon jwenti pi lwen pase kote l rive fasil","Fè mouvman yo dousman, epi pa janm fòse yon jwenti pi lwen pase kote l rive fasil. Rete si gen doulè, epi rapòte l."],["During range of motion, the client's knee stops bending before its usual point. What do you do?","Push a little harder to reach the usual point","Bounce the joint to loosen it","Ask the client to push through it","Stop there; never force a joint past where it moves easily","Move slowly and smoothly, and never force a joint past where it moves easily. Stop if there is pain, and report it."]],["h1112",0,["recent surgery","operasyon resan"],["Kliyan w lan te fè operasyon ranch semèn pase. Plan swen an pa gen ROM pou ranch sa a. Kisa ou fè?","Pa fè ROM sou ranch sa a","Fè yon ti ROM dous sou ranch lan kanmenm","Fè ROM sèlman si kliyan an dakò","Fè plis ROM pou l pa rèd","Pa fè ROM sou kou oswa sou yon jwenti ki fèk opere si plan swen an pa mande l."],["Your client had hip surgery last week. The care plan does not include ROM for that hip. What do you do?","Do not do ROM on that hip","Do gentle ROM on the hip anyway","Do ROM only if the client agrees","Do extra ROM to prevent stiffness","Do not do range of motion on the neck or a recently operated joint unless the care plan calls for it."]]],"12":[["h1202",1,["dehydration","dezidratasyon"],["Ki siy sa yo ka montre dezidratasyon?","Pipi klè an kantite","Bouch sèk ak pipi fonse","Pye anfle","Twòp grangou","Bouch sèk, pipi fonse oswa pi piti pipi, tèt vire ak konfizyon ka siy dezidratasyon. Rapòte yo."],["Which signs can mean dehydration?","Lots of clear urine","Dry mouth and dark urine","Swollen feet","Too much hunger","Dry mouth, dark or less urine, dizziness and confusion can be signs of dehydration. Report them."]],["h1203",0,["refrigerator temperature","tanperati frijidè"],["Ki tanperati frijidè kliyan an dwe genyen?","40°F (4°C) oswa pi ba","50°F (10°C)","60°F (16°C)","Nenpòt tanperati si l frèt","Frijidè a dwe rete nan 40°F (4°C) oswa pi ba pou anpeche mikwòb grandi."],["What temperature should the client's refrigerator be?","40°F (4°C) or below","50°F (10°C)","60°F (16°C)","Any temperature if it feels cold","Keep the refrigerator at 40°F (4°C) or below to slow germ growth."]],["h1204",3,["leftovers","rès manje"],["Konbyen tan rès poul kwit ka rete nan frijidè?","1 semèn, si l kouvri","2 semèn","1 mwa","3 a 4 jou","Rès vyann ak poul kwit bon pou 3 a 4 jou nan frijidè."],["How long can leftover cooked chicken stay in the refrigerator?","1 week, if it is covered","2 weeks","1 month","3 to 4 days","Leftover cooked meat and poultry keep 3 to 4 days in the refrigerator."]],["h1205",1,["fluid restriction","restriksyon likid"],["Kliyan an gen restriksyon likid epi l mande plis dlo pase sa plan an pèmèt. Kisa ou fè?","Ba l sa l mande, paske swaf vle di kò a bezwen dlo","Rete nan limit plan an, ofri l lòt bagay pou soulaje l, epi di enfimyè a","Kache dlo a pou l sispann mande l","Di l pa gen dlo ankò jodi a san esplikasyon, epi soti nan chanm nan","Swiv restriksyon an egzakteman. Ofri swen bouch; bay ti mòso glas sèlman si plan swen an pèmèt sa, paske yo konte kòm likid. Rapòte swaf la."],["The client is on a fluid restriction and asks for more water than the plan allows. What do you do?","Give what they ask for, since thirst means the body needs water","Stay within the plan's limit, offer other comfort, and tell the nurse","Hide the water so they stop asking for it","Say no more water today without explaining, and leave the room","Follow the restriction exactly. Offer mouth care; give ice chips only if the care plan allows, since they count as fluid. Report the thirst."]],["h1206",2,["pocketing food","kenbe manje nan machwè"],["Pandan manje, ou remake kliyan an kenbe manje nan machwè l. Kisa ou fè?","Ba l plis manje vit pou repa a fini alè","Kouche l plat pou l ka repoze apre l fin manje","Fè l sonje kraze ak vale, tcheke bouch li, epi rapòte l","Pa okipe l","Kenbe manje nan machwè ka siy pwoblèm pou vale epi l ka lakòz toufe. Fè l sonje vale, tcheke bouch li, epi rapòte."],["During a meal, you notice the client holding food in their cheeks. What do you do?","Give more food quickly so the meal is finished on time","Lay them down flat so they can rest after eating","Remind them to chew and swallow, check their mouth, and report it","Ignore it","Pocketing food can signal a swallowing problem and cause choking. Remind them to swallow, check the mouth, and report it."]],["hha4",0,["food safety","sekirite manje"],["Manje kwit ki rete dwe antre nan frijidè nan konbyen tan?","Anvan 2 èdtan","Anvan 6 èdtan","Denmen maten","Sèlman si l gen move sant","Mikwòb grandi vit nan tanperati chanm. Mete manje kwit nan frijidè anvan 2 èdtan (1 èdtan si fè plis pase 90°F deyò)."],["Leftover cooked food should go in the refrigerator within how long?","Within 2 hours","Within 6 hours","By the next morning","Only if it smells bad","Bacteria grow fast at room temperature. Refrigerate cooked food within 2 hours (1 hour if it is above 90°F outside)."]],["hha12",0,["refuse","refize"],["Kliyan w lan refize manje manje midi. Ki pi bon repons lan?","Pwopoze yon lòt chwa, respekte desizyon l, epi rapòte sa","Fè l manje kanmenm, paske l bezwen manje a","Retire manje aswè a tou","Di l l ap fè tèt di e l oblije manje","Kliyan yo ka refize. Pwopoze lòt chwa, note konbyen l manje, epi di sipèvizè w si sa kontinye rive."],["Your client refuses to eat lunch. What is the best response?","Offer another choice, respect the decision, and report it","Feed them anyway, because they need the food","Take away dinner too","Tell them they are being difficult and must eat","Clients can refuse. Offer alternatives, note how much they ate, and tell your supervisor if it keeps happening."]],["h1207",0,["low sodium","mwens sèl"],["Kliyan an sou yon rejim ki gen mwens sèl. Ki repa ki pi bon?","Poul fre griye ak bwokoli bouyi san sèl ajoute","Soup poul nan bwat ak biskwit sale bò kote","Yon sandwich janbon ak fwomaj tranche","Nouy enstantane ak sachè epis","Manje fre gen mwens sèl pase manje an bwat, vyann trete ak nouy enstantane. Swiv rejim ki nan plan swen an."],["The client is on a low-sodium diet. Which meal is best?","Fresh grilled chicken with steamed broccoli, no added salt","Canned chicken soup with salted crackers on the side","A deli ham sandwich with sliced cheese","Instant noodles with the seasoning packet","Fresh foods have far less sodium than canned soups, processed meats and instant noodles. Follow the diet in the care plan."]],["h1208",1,["diabetic diet","rejim pou dyabèt"],["Kisa yon rejim pou dyabèt kontwole?","Sèl sèlman","Sik ak karbonidrat","Likid ak dlo sèlman","Pwoteyin sèlman","Yon rejim pou dyabèt kontwole sik ak kantite karbonidrat. Swiv rejim espesyal ki nan plan swen an chak fwa."],["What does a diabetic diet control?","Salt only","Sugar and carbohydrates","Fluids and water only","Protein only","A diabetic diet controls sugar and carbohydrates. Follow any special diet in the care plan every time."]],["h1209",2,["pureed diet","manje moulen"],["Ki moun ki konn bezwen manje mou oswa moulen?","Moun ki sou rejim mwens sèl","Moun ki grangou anpil","Moun ki gen pwoblèm pou kraze oswa vale","Moun ki pa renmen legim","Manje mou oswa moulen (mechanical soft, puree) se pou moun ki gen pwoblèm pou kraze oswa vale."],["Who usually needs soft or pureed food?","People on a low-sodium diet","People who are very hungry","People with chewing or swallowing problems","People who do not like vegetables","Soft or pureed food (mechanical soft, puree) is for people with chewing or swallowing problems."]],["h1210",0,["upright position","chita dwat"],["Kliyan w lan fèk fin manje midi. Kisa l dwe fè apre?","Rete chita dwat pandan yon ti tan","Kouche plat touswit pou l repoze","Kouche sou vant","Panche pou l touche zòtèy li","Fè kliyan an chita dwat pou l manje, epi rete chita kèk tan apre."],["Your client just finished lunch. What should they do next?","Stay sitting upright for a while","Lie flat right away to rest","Lie on their stomach","Bend forward to touch their toes","Sit the client upright to eat, and keep them upright for a while after."]],["h1211",3,["coughing during meals","touse pandan manje"],["Kliyan w lan touse chak fwa l bwè pandan manje. Kisa ou fè?","Ba l pi gwo gòje pou l desann pi vit","Fè l kouche","Sispann ba l bwè pou rès jounen an","Rapòte sa bay enfimyè a","Rapòte touse oswa toufe pandan manje. Sa ka siy yon pwoblèm pou vale."],["Your client coughs every time they drink during meals. What do you do?","Give bigger sips so it goes down faster","Have them lie down","Stop giving drinks for the rest of the day","Report it to the nurse","Report coughing or choking during meals. It can be a sign of a swallowing problem."]],["h1212",1,["self-feeding","manje poukont li"],["Kliyan w lan ka manje poukont li men li dousman. Kisa ki pi bon?","Fè l manje ou menm pou repa a ale pi vit","Ankouraje l manje poukont li epi pa prese l","Retire asyèt la apre 10 minit","Moulen tout manje a pou l ka fini l pi vit","Ankouraje kliyan an manje poukont li otan l kapab, epi pa prese l. Ti mòso, epi kite l kraze ak vale anvan pwochen mòso a."],["Your client can feed themselves but is slow. What is best?","Feed them yourself so the meal goes faster","Encourage them to feed themselves and do not rush them","Take the plate away after 10 minutes","Blend all the food so they can finish it faster","Encourage the client to feed themselves as much as they can, and do not rush. Small bites, and let them chew and swallow before the next one."]]],"13":[["h1302",2,["redness","wouj"],["Gen yon kote wouj sou talon kliyan an ki rete wouj apre w retire presyon an. Kisa ou fè?","Masaj li","Mete yon pansman ou chwazi","Rapòte l bay enfimyè a","Pa fè anyen","Yon kote wouj ki pa disparèt apre w retire presyon ka kòmansman yon blesi presyon. Rapòte l."],["A red area on the client's heel stays red after you relieve the pressure. What do you do?","Massage it","Apply a dressing of your choice","Report it to the nurse","Do nothing","Redness that does not fade after pressure is relieved can be the start of a pressure injury. Report it."]],["h1303",0,["massage","masaj"],["Èske ou dwe masaj yon kote ki wouj sou yon zo?","Non","Wi, pou ogmante sikilasyon","Wi, ak alkòl","Sèlman lannwit","Pa masaj yon kote ki wouj sou yon zo: sa ka fè plis domaj nan tisi a."],["Should you massage a red area over a bone?","No","Yes, to improve circulation","Yes, with alcohol","Only at night","Do not massage a red area over a bone: it can cause more tissue damage."]],["h1304",1,["smooth sheets","dra lis"],["W ap ranje kabann yon kliyan ki rete kouche. Kisa ki pi enpòtan pou po l?","Mete plizyè kouvèti pliye anba l pou kousen","Kenbe dra yo lis, san pli ni miyèt","Mare dra anlè a byen sere sou pye l","Chanje dra yo sèlman yon fwa pa semèn, menm si yo mouye","Pli ak miyèt peze sou po a epi fwote l, sa ka bay blesi presyon. Kenbe dra yo lis, pwòp ak sèk."],["You are making the bed of a client who stays in bed. What matters most for their skin?","Fold extra blankets under them for padding","Keep the sheets smooth, without wrinkles or crumbs","Tuck the top sheet very tight over their feet","Change the sheets only once a week, even if they are wet","Wrinkles and crumbs press into and rub the skin, which can cause pressure injuries. Keep sheets smooth, clean and dry."]],["h1305",1,["diabetes","dyabèt"],["Kliyan w lan gen dyabèt. Kisa ki enpòtan pou pye l?","Koupe kò nan pye l","Gade pye l chak jou epi rapòte blesi oswa fant","Tranpe pye l nan dlo cho lontan","Pa janm gade pye l","Moun ki gen dyabèt ka pa santi blesi nan pye yo. Gade yo chak jou epi rapòte nenpòt blesi."],["Your client has diabetes. What is important for their feet?","Cut the corns on their feet","Check the feet every day and report sores or cracks","Soak the feet in hot water for a long time","Never look at the feet","People with diabetes may not feel foot injuries. Check the feet daily and report any sore."]],["h1306",0,["moisturize","mete krèm"],["Ki kote ou pa dwe mete krèm idratan?","Ant zòtèy yo","Sou janm yo ak jenou yo","Sou bra","Sou do a ak zepòl yo","Krèm ant zòtèy kenbe imidite ki ka fè chanpiyon oswa po a kase. Mete l sou lòt kote ki sèk."],["Where should you NOT apply moisturizing lotion?","Between the toes","On the legs and knees","On the arms","On the back and shoulders","Lotion between the toes traps moisture that can cause fungus or skin breakdown. Apply it to other dry areas."]],["h1307",2,["incontinence","pipi oswa poupou sou li"],["Kliyan an fè pipi sou li nan kabann. Kisa ki pi enpòtan pou po l?","Tann pwochen chanjman ki pwograme","Mete plis dra anba l","Netwaye epi seche po a touswit","Mete pidè sou li san lave","Pipi ak poupou sou po a fè l kase vit. Netwaye epi seche l touswit."],["The client was incontinent in bed. What matters most for their skin?","Wait for the next scheduled change","Add more sheets under them","Clean and dry the skin right away","Apply powder without washing","Urine and stool on the skin break it down quickly. Clean and dry it right away."]],["h1308",1,["oxygen tubing","tib oksijèn"],["Ki kote tib oksijèn ka fè blesi presyon?","Sou talon","Anwo zòrèy yo","Sou jenou","Sou pla pye","Tib oksijèn kouche sou zòrèy yo epi l ka fè presyon. Tcheke zòrèy yo."],["Where can oxygen tubing cause pressure injuries?","On the heels","On the tops of the ears","On the knees","On the soles of the feet","Oxygen tubing rests on the ears and can cause pressure. Check the ears."]],["h1309",2,["skin folds","pli po"],["Pandan w ap tcheke po a, ki lòt kote ou dwe gade apa zo yo?","Figi, men ak bra sèlman","Sèlman kote kliyan an montre w","Anba tete, nan pli po ak ant zòtèy","Sèlman kote rad oswa soulye sere","Gade sou zo yo, epi tou anba tete, nan pli po ak ant zòtèy."],["During a skin check, which areas should you look at besides the bony areas?","Only the face, hands and arms","Only where the client points","Under the breasts, in skin folds and between the toes","Only where clothing or shoes feel tight","Check over the bones, and also under the breasts, in skin folds and between the toes."]],["h1310",0,["skin change","chanjman po"],["Ou remake yon kote sou ranch kliyan an ki pi cho epi pi di pase po ki bò kote l. Kisa ou fè?","Rapòte l bay enfimyè a","Masaje l pou l vin mou","Kouvri l ak yon bandaj sere","Pa okipe l si l pa wouj","Yon kote ki cho, di oswa mou, ki diferan de po ki bò kote l, se yon chanjman pou w rapòte, menm si l pa wouj."],["You notice an area on the client's hip that feels warmer and harder than the skin around it. What do you do?","Report it to the nurse","Massage it to soften it","Cover it with a tight bandage","Ignore it if it is not red","An area that feels warm, hard or soft compared with the skin around it is a change to report, even if it is not red."]]],"14":[["h1402",2,["in-service training","fòmasyon kontinyèl"],["Konbyen èdtan fòmasyon kontinyèl (in-service) yon ed swen a domisil bezwen chak ane?","4 èdtan","8 èdtan","12 èdtan","24 èdtan","Règ federal la mande omwen 12 èdtan fòmasyon kontinyèl chak 12 mwa."],["How many hours of in-service training does a home health aide need each year?","4 hours","8 hours","12 hours","24 hours","The federal rule requires at least 12 hours of in-service training every 12 months."]],["h1403",0,["24-month lapse","24 mwa san travay"],["Ou pa t travay kòm ed pou lajan pandan 24 mwa youn dèyè lòt. Kisa ou dwe fè anvan w retounen?","Refè yon pwogram fòmasyon oswa evalyasyon konpetans","Anyen; sètifika w toujou valab pou tout lavi","Fè 2 èdtan fòmasyon kontinyèl","Jwenn yon lèt referans nan dènye ajans ou","Apre 24 mwa youn dèyè lòt san travay peye, ou dwe refè yon pwogram anvan w bay swen ankò."],["You have not worked as a paid aide for 24 months in a row. What must you do before returning?","Complete a training or competency evaluation program again","Nothing; your certificate is still valid for life","Take 2 hours of in-service training","Get a reference letter from your last agency","After 24 consecutive months without paid aide work, you must complete a program again before giving care."]],["h1404",2,["topical cream","krèm pou po"],["Ki travay sa yo yon ed gen dwa fè ak medikaman?","Bay yon piki ensilin si kliyan an montre w kijan","Ranpli bwat grenn semèn kliyan an ak boutèy yo","Mete yon krèm san preskripsyon sou po ki pa blese jan yo montre w","Deside si kliyan an bezwen yon grenn pou doulè","Mete yon krèm san preskripsyon sou po ki pa blese, dapre enstriksyon, se youn nan èd pasif gid federal la bay kòm egzanp."],["Which of these may an aide do with medications?","Give an insulin injection if the client shows you how","Fill the client's weekly pill organizer from the bottles","Apply a non-prescription cream to unbroken skin as instructed","Decide whether the client needs a pain pill","Applying a non-prescription cream to unbroken skin, per instructions, is one of the passive tasks federal guidance lists as an example."]],["h1405",1,["state law","lwa leta"],["Règ leta w la sou fòmasyon ed pi sevè pase règ federal la. Ki règ ou swiv?","Règ federal la","Règ ki pi sevè a","Sa ou pito a","Okenn","Lè yon règ leta pi sevè, se li ki aplike. Lè règ federal la pi sevè, se li ki aplike."],["Your state's aide training rule is stricter than the federal rule. Which do you follow?","The federal rule","The stricter rule","Whichever you prefer","Neither","When a state rule is stricter, it applies. When the federal rule is stricter, it applies."]],["h1406",0,["supervisory visit","vizit siveyans"],["Kliyan an resevwa swen enfimyè. Chak konbyen tan yon RN oswa terapis dwe evalye swen ou bay?","Omwen chak 14 jou","Chak 6 mwa","Yon fwa pa ane","Sèlman si fanmi an plenyen","Lè kliyan an resevwa swen teknik, evalyasyon siveyans lan fèt omwen chak 14 jou. Ed la pa oblije la."],["The client receives nursing care. How often must an RN or therapist review the care you give?","At least every 14 days","Every 6 months","Once a year","Only if the family complains","When the client gets skilled services, the supervisory review happens at least every 14 days. The aide does not need to be present."]],["h1407",2,["training","fòmasyon"],["Ajans lan vle w fè yon nouvo travay ou pa t janm aprann. Kisa ki dwe fèt anvan?","Ou eseye l pou wè","Yon lòt ed esplike w pa telefòn","Ajans lan ba w fòmasyon pou travay sa a","Ou li sou entènèt","Ajans lan responsab pou fòme ed yo pou konpetans ki pa nan lis debaz la, anvan yo fè yo."],["Your agency wants you to do a new task you were never taught. What must happen first?","You try it and see","Another aide explains it by phone","The agency trains you for that task","You read about it online","The agency is responsible for training aides on skills beyond the basic list before they perform them."]],["h1408",1,["nurse aide registry","rejis ed enfimyè"],["Ou se yon CNA ki an règ sou rejis eta a. Èske w satisfè kondisyon fòmasyon pou travay kòm ed swen a domisil?","Non, ou dwe refè 75 èdtan","Wi","Sèlman si w gen 5 ane eksperyans","Sèlman nan lopital","Yon ed enfimyè ki fini yon pwogram apwouve pa leta epi ki an règ sou rejis la satisfè kondisyon fòmasyon ed swen a domisil."],["You are a CNA in good standing on the state registry. Do you meet the training requirement to work as a home health aide?","No, you must redo 75 hours","Yes","Only with 5 years of experience","Only in hospitals","A nurse aide who completed a state-approved program and is in good standing on the registry meets the home health aide training requirement."]],["h1409",2,["pill organizer","bwat grenn semèn"],["Kliyan an mande w ranpli bwat grenn semèn li. Kisa ou fè?","Ranpli l ak atansyon apati boutèy yo","Ranpli l si fanmi an tcheke l apre","Pa ranpli l; di enfimyè a","Ranpli sèlman dòz maten yo","Ed swen pa ka ranpli bwat grenn semèn nan, chwazi oswa chanje dòz, ni bay piki. Di enfimyè a."],["The client asks you to fill their weekly pill organizer. What do you do?","Fill it carefully from the bottles","Fill it if the family checks it afterward","Do not fill it; tell the nurse","Fill only the morning doses","Aides may not fill the weekly pill organizer, choose or change a dose, or give injections. Tell the nurse."]],["h1410",0,["missed dose","dòz rate"],["Ou remake grenn maten kliyan an toujou nan bwat la a lè manje midi. Kisa ou fè?","Rapòte dòz rate a bay enfimyè a","Ba l grenn maten yo ak manje midi a","Jete grenn yo","Ba l doub dòz aswè a","Rapòte si kliyan an rate dòz, refize medikaman, oswa gen yon reyaksyon. Pa janm deside oswa chanje yon dòz poukont ou."],["At lunchtime you notice your client's morning pills are still in the organizer. What do you do?","Report the missed dose to the nurse","Give the morning pills with lunch","Throw the pills away","Give a double dose tonight","Report if the client misses doses, refuses a medication, or has a reaction. Never decide on or change a dose yourself."]],["h1411",1,["self-administration","pran medikaman pou kont li"],["Kisa sa vle di lè yon kliyan pran medikaman li pou kont li?","Ed la retire grenn yo epi bay chak dòz","Kliyan an oswa yon moun k ap okipe l jere estokaj, dòz, lè ak renouvèlman","Yon enfimyè vin lakay la chak jou pou bay chak dòz","Famasi a deside ki lè kliyan an pran chak grenn","Pran medikaman pou kont li vle di kliyan an (oswa moun k ap okipe l) jere tout bagay: kenbe medikaman yo an sekirite, bon dòz la, a lè, epi rele famasi a."],["What does it mean that a client self-administers their medications?","The aide takes the pills out and gives each dose","The client or a caregiver handles storage, doses, timing and refills","A nurse comes to the home every day to give each dose","The pharmacy decides when the client takes each pill","Self-administration means the client (or their caregiver) manages everything: storing medications safely, the right dose, the right time, and calling the pharmacy."]],["h1412",3,["competency evaluation","evalyasyon konpetans"],["Pandan evalyasyon konpetans ou, yo ba w «pa satisfezan» nan de domèn obligatwa. Kisa k rive?","Ou pase, men ou dwe pratike konpetans sa yo","Ou pase si egzamen ekri w la te bon","Ou ka travay nan domèn sa yo ak yon kòlèg","Ou pa pase evalyasyon an","Si w gen «pa satisfezan» nan plis pase yon sèl domèn obligatwa, ou pa pase evalyasyon an."],["During your competency evaluation, you are rated unsatisfactory in two required areas. What happens?","You pass, but must practice those skills","You pass if your written test was strong","You can work in those areas with a coworker","You do not pass the evaluation","If you are rated unsatisfactory in more than one required area, you do not pass the evaluation."]],["h1413",0,["retraining","fòmasyon ankò"],["Pandan yon vizit siveyans, enfimyè a jwenn yon pwoblèm nan fason w fè transfè. Kisa ki dwe rive?","Ou fè fòmasyon ankò ak yon nouvo evalyasyon sou konpetans sa a ak konpetans ki gen rapò","Anyen pa bezwen fèt si pèsonn pa blese","Ou resevwa yon lèt avètisman sèlman","Ou dwe refè tout pwogram fòmasyon 75 èdtan an","Si yo jwenn yon pwoblèm nan swen ou, ou dwe fè fòmasyon ankò ak yon nouvo evalyasyon pou konpetans sa a ak konpetans ki gen rapò."],["During a supervisory visit, the nurse finds a problem with how you transfer clients. What must happen?","You are retrained and re-evaluated on that skill and related skills","Nothing needs to happen if no one was hurt","You get a warning letter only","You must repeat the whole 75-hour training program","If a problem is found in your care, you must be retrained and re-evaluated on that skill and related skills."]]]};
